### OrderFlow API examples
# Works with the IntelliJ HTTP Client and the VS Code REST Client extension.
# Start the services first (see README). Run the requests from top to bottom.
# Orders are confirmed asynchronously: GET the order a moment later to see its final status.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@inventoryUrl = http://localhost:8081
@authUrl = http://localhost:9000
# Fill in locally and do not commit: the client secrets you chose in .env, the access_token
# returned by one of the token requests below and the id of an order you placed.
@operatorSecret =
@readerSecret =
@token =
@orderId =
# Use a fresh value for every new order attempt; repeat it only to retry the same order.
@idempotencyKey = 0f8b6c52-3f0e-4a8e-9d43-6a1e2b7c9d10

### Get an operator token (scopes orderflow.read and orderflow.operate)
POST {{authUrl}}/oauth2/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=client_credentials&scope=orderflow.read%20orderflow.operate&client_id=orderflow-operator&client_secret={{operatorSecret}}

### Get a read-only token: writes with it answer 403
POST {{authUrl}}/oauth2/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=client_credentials&scope=orderflow.read&client_id=orderflow-reader&client_secret={{readerSecret}}

### Register a product with 5 units on hand
POST {{inventoryUrl}}/api/v1/products
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sku": "MUG-BLUE-01",
  "name": "Blue ceramic mug",
  "onHandQuantity": 5
}

### Register a product that is almost sold out
POST {{inventoryUrl}}/api/v1/products
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sku": "LAMP-DESK-01",
  "name": "Desk lamp",
  "onHandQuantity": 1
}

### Check stock levels (onHand, reserved and available)
GET {{inventoryUrl}}/api/v1/products/MUG-BLUE-01
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### List products whose SKU starts with a prefix
GET {{inventoryUrl}}/api/v1/products?skuPrefix=MUG-&page=0&size=20
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Place an order: it is PENDING until the inventory service reserves the stock (then CONFIRMED)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{idempotencyKey}}

{
  "channel": "WEB_STORE",
  "currency": "BRL",
  "items": [
    { "sku": "MUG-BLUE-01", "quantity": 2, "unitPrice": 59.90 }
  ]
}

### Retry the same request: same order, header Idempotent-Replayed: true, no extra reservation
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{idempotencyKey}}

{
  "channel": "WEB_STORE",
  "currency": "BRL",
  "items": [
    { "sku": "MUG-BLUE-01", "quantity": 2, "unitPrice": 59.90 }
  ]
}

### Reuse the key with a different payload: 422 idempotency-key-reused
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{idempotencyKey}}

{
  "channel": "WEB_STORE",
  "currency": "BRL",
  "items": [
    { "sku": "MUG-BLUE-01", "quantity": 3, "unitPrice": 59.90 }
  ]
}

### Ask for more than is available: the inventory rejects it, the order becomes REJECTED and nothing is reserved
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: 7d2e9a41-5b6c-4f3d-8e1a-2c9b7a6d5e40

{
  "channel": "MARKETPLACE",
  "currency": "BRL",
  "items": [
    { "sku": "MUG-BLUE-01", "quantity": 1, "unitPrice": 59.90 },
    { "sku": "LAMP-DESK-01", "quantity": 2, "unitPrice": 149.00 }
  ]
}

### Invalid request: every invalid field is reported in one problem detail
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: 1b4c7e2a-9d3f-4a6b-8c5e-0f2d1a3b4c59

{
  "channel": "web",
  "currency": "BRL",
  "items": [
    { "sku": "MUG-BLUE-01", "quantity": 0, "unitPrice": 59.999 }
  ]
}

### List the most recent orders, optionally by status and channel
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders?status=CONFIRMED&page=0&size=20
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Get one order and see whether the inventory confirmed or rejected it
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders/{{orderId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Cancel an order; the inventory releases its stock when it receives OrderCancelled
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders/{{orderId}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
